**Decision for you:** syside 0.11.0 is proprietary and needs a license key (`SYSIDE_LICENSE_KEY`). You have to put it in the ST-3 run environment. Without it the parse check records the gap SYSIDE_LICENSE_MISSING, and ST-4 can't start. syside documents no `check` command, so the parse check uses its Python `load_model` call instead.

I did not install or run the real syside: that needs the supply-chain scan receipt and your key, and both happen when ST-3 runs. The Orchestrator still has to record the new digest against SD-031 in `journey.json`.

